  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fighting Corruption Globally</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Fighting Corruption Globally programme will address transnational grand corruption by supporting efforts to put in place the tools and capabilities to prevent corrupt actors from stealing and moving significant financial resources around the world, and to hold them to account when transnational corruption does occur. 
The programme will do this by: 
&#x2022;	Enabling governments, civil society, the private sector and law enforcement to use high-quality beneficial ownership data to prevent or identify cases of grand corruption; 
&#x2022;	Improving the effectiveness of international law enforcement to increase the volume of recovered assets; 
&#x2022;	Equipping the Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office&#x2019;s (FCDO) country networks, FCDO and other actors with evidence and learning for effective policy and programming on anti-corruption.</narrative>
  </description>
